-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Gryzor
  Publisher   Ocean, 1987
  Version     1.3

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Gryzor (1987)(Ocean)(48K-128K).z80
  MD5         fdab5fb61b2cb01ce38edcfa85ea9e80

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The commando, the runners, riflemen, gunners, turrets, shots and
              blasts redrawn in full colour and lined up on the original
              figures, so hits land where you see them. Off by default. A
              painted set, colourist not named.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same file;
              probe 0xA439 (the player's controls read, once per game update);
              input keyed to updates; both runs in lockstep at every update in
              all 15 trials)

  Changes     1.0: figures and bullets as Next sprites; black outline;
              Sinclair's 48K ROM as the alt ROM; hooks at 28 MHz restoring the
              game's speed; R kept, so the game's random numbers are the
              original's; the original's pace kept by a pace limiter and
              prepared sprite patterns
              1.1: rebuilt on NexClash's shared pace code; plays at the
              original's pace as 1.0 did
              1.2: Starts with the Next's DivMMC automap switched off:
              NextZXOS leaves it on, and on current cores that could crash the
              game or spoil its drawing
              1.3: Enhanced colours, a menu choice off by default: the
              commando, the enemies, the turrets, the shots and the blasts
              redrawn in full colour, lined up on the original figures so hits
              land where you see them

  Note        Keys: hold 0 on the menu to start (the menu checks the keyboard
              every few frames); cursor keys 5 left, 8 right, 7 jump, 6 down,
              0 fire. The player, enemies and bullets are Next sprites with a
              black outline (the owner's choice), so they show one colour
              across the jungle's bands; scenery, stars, objects and text keep
              the original's colours. Enhanced, on the menu, redraws every
              figure in full colour. Plays at the original's pace (hooks at 28
              MHz, your speed restored) and gives the same enemies for the
              same keys. Known issues: in the yellow forest the black outline
              meets the forest's black pattern, so figures read less well
              there; while the scenery scrolls, a figure can show a frame
              behind it now and then; in Enhanced the overhead rifle and one
              diagonal aim are drawn 4 lines higher than the original's.
              Missing: this is the 48K form, so the first section only and no
              128K music; the cheats are the archive's, checked on a simulator
              only; not yet checked: Kempston and define keys.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to enemies touch
   3  Immune to enemy fire

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

